# Internationalisation

Every visible string flows through one [`MessageFormatter`](/api-reference/index/type-aliases/MessageFormatter). Three sources are supported out of the box; for anything else, write your own formatter function.

## Source 1 — built-in `messageConfig`

The default. Strings live on the config in a structured object. `messageFormatter: 'config'` is implicit when `messageConfig` is set.

```typescript
const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
    type: 'userData',
    columnProperties: { /* ... */ },
    dataUniquePropertyKey: 'id',
    messageFormatter: 'config',
    messageConfig: {
        id:        { label: 'Id' },
        userName:  { label: 'Username', format: '@{value}' },
        firstName: { label: 'First name' },
        gender:    {
            label: 'Gender',
            enumValue: { male: 'Male', female: 'Female' }
        },
        pagination: { previous: 'Previous', next: 'Next', first: 'First', last: 'Last' },
        search: { placeholder: 'Search', ariaLabel: 'Search users' },
        actions: { selectedCount: '{count} selected', edit: 'Edit', delete: 'Delete' },
        export:  { button: 'Export', title: 'Export rows', /* ... */ }
    }
};
```

[`MessageConfig`](/api-reference/index/type-aliases/MessageConfig) is deep-merged onto the built-in English defaults, so partial configs work — set only the keys you want to override. Per-action labels live under `actions.<key>` and resolve through the same formatter.

`{value}` and `{count}` are interpolation placeholders — the library replaces them with the row value and selection count respectively.

## Source 2 — svelte-i18n

Pass the `format` store directly. Every message id is prefixed and looked up through svelte-i18n's normal resolution.

```typescript
import { format, addMessages, init, getLocaleFromNavigator } from 'svelte-i18n';
import localeEn from './locales/en.json';
import localeDe from './locales/de.json';

addMessages('en', localeEn);
addMessages('de', localeDe);
init({ fallbackLocale: 'en', initialLocale: getLocaleFromNavigator() });

const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
    type: 'userData',
    columnProperties: { /* ... */ },
    dataUniquePropertyKey: 'id',
    messageFormatter: format,
    messageFormatterPrefix: ''       // optional — e.g. 'datatable.' if your bundle nests these
};
```

Per-column labels are looked up at `dataTable.<config.type>.<key>.label`. Pagination/search/actions/export live at top-level keys (`pagination.next`, `search.placeholder`, ...). Mirror the `messageConfig` shape inside your locale JSON:

```json
{
    "search":     { "placeholder": "Search", "ariaLabel": "Search" },
    "pagination": { "previous": "Previous", "next": "Next", "first": "First", "last": "Last" },
    "dataTable": {
        "userData": {
            "id":       { "label": "Id" },
            "userName": { "label": "Username", "format": "@{value}" },
            "gender":   { "label": "Gender", "enumValue": { "male": "Male", "female": "Female" } }
        }
    }
}
```

## Source 3 — custom `MessageFormatter`

Anything that matches the signature works — `react-intl`-style ICU formatters, a `Map` lookup, even hard-coded translation tables.

```typescript
import type { MessageFormatter } from 'svelte-advanced-datatable';

const formatter: MessageFormatter = (id, opts) => {
    const raw = bundle[locale]?.[id] ?? opts?.default ?? id;
    return interpolate(raw, opts?.values ?? {});
};

const config: DataTableConfig<UserData> = {
    // ...
    messageFormatter: formatter
};
```

Use [`createMessageFormatter`](/api-reference/index/functions/createMessageFormatter) when you need a `MessageFormatter` instance built from the resolved config (e.g. inside a custom exporter `run` callback).

## Options

| Option                   | Type                                                     | Description                                                                                                | Default     |
|:-------------------------|:---------------------------------------------------------|:-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|:------------|
| `messageFormatter`       | `'config' \| svelteI18nFormat \| MessageFormatter`       | Source of all strings.                                                                                      | `'config'`  |
| `messageFormatterPrefix` | `string`                                                 | Prefix prepended to every message id; only applies to external formatters such as svelte-i18n.              | `''`        |
| `messageConfig`          | `MessageConfig<Data>`                                    | Static strings. Required for `messageFormatter: 'config'`; ignored otherwise.                              | —           |

